# Theme System — Folder Rules

> Pre-edit hook injects the full `RULES.md` chain when editing Vue/TS. Read `app.rnc/src/styles/theme/RULES.md` manually when editing `colors.css`.

## Brand contract

- **`colors.css`** is the single source of truth for hex values — primary `#c0e021` (500), surface `#888b8d` (500), ink `#141413` (900)
- **`theme.ts`** reads CSS vars only — no duplicate hex literals (except `surface.0` white)
- Palettes: `primary`, `surface`, `ink` — never `lime`, `gray`, `black`

## Contributor rules

- Never hardcode hex in `.vue` files — use Tailwind utilities or `var(--color-*)`
- Never use built-in Tailwind palettes (`sky`, `emerald`, `gray`, etc.) — use semantic tokens
- State colors: `success`, `info`, `warn`, `danger` — not `green`, `red`, `amber`

## Forking

To retheme app.rnc: change hex in `colors.css` only — no component edits needed.
